<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Ireland</h1><p class="st-meta">1937 CE – present · capital Dublin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The sovereign Irish state established under the 1937 Constitution, which became a republic in 1949 and an EU member in 1973.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-ireland">Constitution of Ireland</a>, drafted under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eamon-de-valera">Eamon de Valera</a> and approved by referendum in 1937, replaced the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/irish-free-state">Irish Free State</a> with a state named Ireland, or Eire, with an elected President, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douglas-hyde">Douglas Hyde</a> being the first. It claimed the whole island but applied its laws to twenty-six counties.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Ireland stayed neutral in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and declared itself a republic in 1949, leaving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-nations">Commonwealth</a>. It is a parliamentary democracy with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oireachtas">Oireachtas</a> and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taoiseach">Taoiseach</a>. Long dominated by the Catholic Church and emigration, it changed through economic openness, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-economic-community">EEC</a> membership in 1973 and the 'Celtic Tiger' boom of the 1990s.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/good-friday-agreement">Good Friday Agreement</a> of 1998 replaced its territorial claim with an aspiration to unity by consent. Referendums legalised divorce, same-sex marriage in 2015 and abortion in 2018, and Ireland is a member of the eurozone.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ireland.jpg" alt="Ireland" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Éire · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ireland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1937 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd>